28.5.3. Using Probes
The example below shows a DTrace script for analyzing transaction counts in the system, as an alternative
to snapshotting pg_stat_database before and after a performance test:
#!/usr/sbin/dtrace -qs
postgresql$1:::transaction-start
{
      @start["Start"] = count();
      self->ts  = timestamp;
}
postgresql$1:::transaction-abort
{
      @abort["Abort"] = count();
}
postgresql$1:::transaction-commit
/self->ts/
{
      @commit["Commit"] = count();
      @time["Total time (ns)"] = sum(timestamp - self->ts);
      self->ts=0;
}
