36.4.5.2. Composite Types
Composite types are not directly supported in ECPG, but an easy workaround is possible. The available
workarounds are similar to the ones described for arrays above: Either access each attribute separately or
use the external string representation.
For the following examples, assume the following type and table:
CREATE TYPE comp_t AS (intval integer, textval varchar(32));
CREATE TABLE t4 (compval comp_t);
INSERT INTO t4 VALUES ( (256, 'PostgreSQL') );
The most obvious solution is to access each attribute separately. The following program retrieves data
from the example table by selecting each attribute of the type comp_t separately:
EXEC SQL BEGIN DECLARE SECTION;
int intval;
varchar textval[33];
EXEC SQL END DECLARE SECTION;
/* Put each element of the composite type column in the SELECT list.
 */
EXEC SQL DECLARE cur1 CURSOR FOR SELECT (compval).intval,
 (compval).textval FROM t4;
