Another workaround is avoiding the direct use of the user-defined types in ECPG and instead create a
function or cast that converts between the user-defined type and a primitive type that ECPG can handle.
Note, however, that type casts, especially implicit ones, should be introduced into the type system very
carefully.
For example,
CREATE FUNCTION create_complex(r double, i double) RETURNS complex
LANGUAGE SQL
IMMUTABLE
AS $$ SELECT $1 * complex '(1,0')' + $2 * complex '(0,1)' $$;
