Commit or roll back the current transaction. This can only be called in a procedure or anonymous code
block (DO command) called from the top level. (Note that it is not possible to run the SQL commands
COMMIT or ROLLBACK via spi_exec_query or similar. It has to be done using these functions.)
After a transaction is ended, a new transaction is automatically started, so there is no separate function
for that.
Here is an example:
CREATE PROCEDURE transaction_test1()
LANGUAGE plperl
AS $$
foreach my $i (0..9) {
    spi_exec_query("INSERT INTO test1 (a) VALUES ($i)");
    if ($i % 2 == 0) {
        spi_commit();
    } else {
        spi_rollback();
    }
}
$$;
CALL transaction_test1();
