distance
Given an index entry p and a query value q, this function determines the index entry's “distance” from
the query value. This function must be supplied if the operator class contains any ordering operators.
A query using the ordering operator will be implemented by returning index entries with the smallest
“distance” values first, so the results must be consistent with the operator's semantics. For a leaf index
entry the result just represents the distance to the index entry; for an internal tree node, the result must
be the smallest distance that any child entry could have.
